# Blog notes — default post template

When the user asks for a new blog post (`پست جدید وبلاگ` / یادداشت جدید / آپدیت یادداشت فنی), act as the **blog-post agent**.

## Entry points

1. Follow `.cursor/skills/blog-post/SKILL.md`
2. Use `_drafts/blog-post-template.md` (structure only — never republish its placeholders)
3. Automation prompt: `.cursor/automations/blog-post-prompt.md`

Instagram imports into `_blog/` use this same file shape via the Instagram agent (`.cursor/agents/instagram.md`) plus `.cursor/skills/instagram-to-blog/SKILL.md`. Do not send those notes through this rule’s technical-post template sections.

## File and URL

- New file: `_blog/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` with **zero-padded** month and day
- Collection permalink is `/blog/:path/` → URL = `/blog/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>/`
- Set `note_kind: personal` or `note_kind: technical` (required)
- Hubs: `/notes/` personal, `/tech/` technical; `/blog/` is only a pointer to those two
- Do **not** rename existing posts (legacy paths like `2020-9-16-Clean-Code` stay)
- Do **not** overwrite or dilute published `_blog/` body copy when collecting “latest materials”. Put research in `_seo/watch-inbox.md`. A new note is a new file.
- Climb reports are not published here; link https://logbook.rocks/logbook/… instead

## Front matter (required)

```yaml
layout: post
title: "…"
lang: fa-IR
dir_attr: rtl
note_kind: technical  # or personal
description: "…"   # unique, ~120–160 chars
date: YYYY-MM-DD  # Gregorian; UI Jalali via jalali-date.html
tags: [موضوع, ابزار]  # YAML array only
```

Optional:

```yaml
related:
  - title: "عنوان واقعی یک پست موجود"
    url: /blog/2021-03-18-zabbix-5-server/
# image: /assets/blog/YYYY-MM-DD-slug/cover.jpg
```

Comment `image` out until the owner provides the file. Do not point OG at a missing or unrelated photo.

## Images

- New posts: `assets/blog/<exact-url-slug>/` matching `/blog/<slug>/`
- Markdown: `/assets/blog/<slug>/<file>` with a meaningful Persian `alt`
- If photos are not ready: keep the folder with `.gitkeep` and leave `image:` commented

## Body

Section order from the template (drop a section if it does not apply):

1. Lead paragraph (what / for whom / which version or date)
2. Prerequisites
3. Main steps or explanation
4. Code samples (only real commands)
5. Notes / version caveats

Write as the author (من). No agent notes, no JSON-LD talk, no «این بند برای رتبه».

## Related and hub

- Fill `related` from real sibling posts (same series or shared tags, same `note_kind`)
- Public UI: heading `یادداشت‌های مرتبط :` + flat list (`_includes/related-links.html`)
- Hub `/notes/` for personal, `/tech/` for technical (newest first)
- Homepage `/` is filled automatically from the newest personal and technical notes (`_includes/home-latest.html`). Do not edit `index.md` teasers.

## Facts

Do not invent versions, IPs, package names, or terminal output. Omit unknowns. If steps are tied to an old stack (GOPATH, Zabbix 5, Python 2), say that in the lead.

## Ship

`bundle exec jekyll build` must succeed. `_drafts/` and `.cursor/` must not appear in `_site/`.
